@startuml

title Shop database - Purchases

!include ./_common.puml

enum PaymentStatusEnum {
    unpaid
    partially_paid
    paid
    overpaid
    refunded
}

enum PurchaseStatus {
    draft
    ordered
    partially_received
    received
    completed
    canceled
    partially_returned
    returned
}

entity Purchase {
    * id: int
    * version: int
    --
    * number: string(255)
    * status: PurchaseStatus
    * currency: Currency
    * exchangeRateToBase: decimal(18, 8)
    supplierNameSnapshot: string(255)?
    supplierPhoneSnapshot: string(255)?
    supplierEmailSnapshot: string(255)?
    invoiceNumber: string(255)?
    documentDate: DateTimeImmutable?
    comment: text?
    * totalAmount: decimal(14, 4)
    * totalAmountBase: decimal(14, 4)
    deliveryCost: decimal(14, 4)?
    deliveryCostBase: decimal(14, 4)?
    canceledAt: DateTimeImmutable?
    * paidAmountBase: decimal(14, 4)
    * paymentStatus: PaymentStatusEnum
    paidAt: DateTimeImmutable?
    * createdAt: DateTimeImmutable
    * updatedAt: DateTimeImmutable
    * store: Store
    createdBy: User?
    updatedBy: User?
    canceledBy: User?
    supplier: Supplier?
}

entity PurchaseEntry {
    * id: int
    --
    * quantity: decimal(14, 4)
    receivedQuantity: decimal(14, 4)?
    returnedQuantity: decimal(14, 4)?
    * unitCost: decimal(14, 4)
    * unitCostBase: decimal(14, 4)
    deliveryCost: decimal(14, 4)?
    deliveryCostBase: decimal(14, 4)?
    * totalCost: decimal(14, 4)
    * totalCostBase: decimal(14, 4)
    salePrice: decimal(14, 4)?
    salePriceBase: decimal(14, 4)?
    * productNameSnapshot: string(255)
    * productCodeSnapshot: string(255)
    * unitCodeSnapshot: string(50)
    * unitNameSnapshot: string(255)
    * purchase: Purchase
    * product: Product
    * warehouse: Warehouse
}


Store ||--o{ Purchase : creates
Currency ||--o{ Purchase : purchase currency
Supplier |o--o{ Purchase : supplies
PurchaseStatus ||--o{ Purchase : controls
PaymentStatusEnum ||--o{ Purchase : payment state
Purchase ||--o{ PurchaseEntry : has
Purchase |o--o{ Payment : paid by
Purchase |o--o{ PaymentHistory : shows payment events
Purchase ||--o{ InventoryDocument : generates stock docs
Product ||--o{ PurchaseEntry : purchased as
Warehouse ||--o{ PurchaseEntry : received into
PurchaseEntry |o--o{ WarehouseStockBatch : may create batches
PurchaseEntry |o--o{ InventoryDocumentLine : receives/returns

note right of Purchase
  Supplier is optional to allow quick/manual purchases.
  createdBy/updatedBy/canceledBy are audit fields for admin accountability.
  canceledAt should be filled when status becomes canceled.
  supplierNameSnapshot/supplierPhoneSnapshot/supplierEmailSnapshot store supplier data at purchase time.

  currency stores the original purchase currency.
  exchangeRateToBase is a snapshot: 1 purchase currency = X Store.baseCurrency.
  totalAmount/deliveryCost are in original currency; *Base fields are in Store.baseCurrency.
  The visible admin history merges status history with linked PaymentHistory events.
end note

note right of PaymentHistory
  PaymentHistory rows are append-only financial timeline events.
  They are displayed together with purchase status history in the purchase admin history,
  but Payment remains the financial source of truth.
end note

note right of PurchaseStatus
  Recommended purchase flow:
  draft -> ordered -> partially_received -> received -> completed.

  partially_returned/returned are used when goods are returned to supplier.
  canceled is for purchases stopped before they are completed.
end note

note right of PurchaseEntry
  Purchase line.
  Stores snapshot of product name, code, unit code/name, quantity, unit cost, delivery cost and optional planned sale price.
  Monetary fields without Base suffix are in Purchase.currency. Base fields are in Store.baseCurrency.

  receivedQuantity and returnedQuantity are denormalized progress/cache fields
  for fast UI and filtering. Source of truth is InventoryDocumentLine + posted StockMovement.
  If cache becomes inconsistent, recalculate it from posted inventory documents.

  Partial receipts are allowed:
  one PurchaseEntry can be linked to multiple InventoryDocumentLine rows over time.
  Open quantity = quantity - receivedQuantity + returnedQuantity, depending on final business rules.

  InventoryDocumentLine and WarehouseStockBatch are created when purchase is posted/received.
end note

@enduml
